message: "If you use or reference this research, please cite the Candidate v1.0 baseline."

title: "NOX: A Safety-Critical Containment Architecture for Hostile Agentic Artificial Intelligence — Consolidated Architecture and Assurance Baseline"

type: report

authors:
  - family-names: "Heese"
    given-names: "Donald"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-9779-2432"

version: "Candidate v1.0"

date-released: 2026-11-11

repository-code: "https://github.com/HeeseDonald/NOX"

url: "https://github.com/HeeseDonald/NOX"

license: CC-BY-4.0

abstract: >-
  NOX is a candidate safety-critical containment architecture and
  assurance baseline for hostile or potentially hostile agentic
  artificial intelligence. The work defines a hazard-first six-zone
  architecture, an independent safety authority, minimal-by-default
  design requirements, causal-isolation requirements, safe-state
  controls, hardware and software assurance requirements, verification
  obligations, and experiment-authorization gates. Candidate v1.0 does
  not represent an implemented, independently validated, certified, or
  operationally authorized containment system.

keywords:
  - hostile agentic AI
  - AI containment
  - AI safety
  - AI security
  - safety-critical systems
  - systems architecture
  - deterministic control
  - formal verification
  - hardware assurance
  - causal isolation
  - agentic AI governance

